      "content": "That's helpful, but to be honest, I feel like the critique of the dissent is a bit soft. In my seminar, the professor is going to push us to really tear down the dissent's logic on the privacy issue. Can you be more direct? Why is their invocation of 'privacy' considered a legal error rather than just a different interpretation? Essentially, I need you to explain how the dissent's logic fails the test of constitutional law.",
